rue,"attachedFrame":"BvuiC-C3fXnVMvtP4NEZ7"},{"id":"NMWDC3Grm---ZOAb3e54-","fillColor":"#607d8b","height":120,"position":{"x":10360,"y":5010},"type":"shape","kind":"rectangle","width":140,"text":"","textFontFamily":"Inter","stickyNote":true,"attachedFrame":"BvuiC-C3fXnVMvtP4NEZ7"},{"id":"gSgl2zwMmEITOAFaa-7Dc","fillColor":"#607d8b","height":120,"position":{"x":10340,"y":5030},"type":"shape","kind":"rectangle","width":140,"text":"","textFontFamily":"Inter","stickyNote":true,"attachedFrame":"BvuiC-C3fXnVMvtP4NEZ7"},{"id":"vFSUEaRq0-wIZZVthdWUH","fillColor":"#607d8b","height":120,"position":{"x":10320,"y":5050},"type":"shape","kind":"rectangle","width":140,"text":"","textFontFamily":"Inter","stickyNote":true,"attachedFrame":"BvuiC-C3fXnVMvtP4NEZ7"},{"id":"CGlkeeVsqu7RFTzrOJt6-","fillColor":"#607d8b","height":120,"position":{"x":10300,"y":5070},"type":"shape","kind":"rectangle","width":140,"text":"","textFontFamily":"Inter","stickyNote":true,"attachedFrame":"BvuiC-C3fXnVMvtP4NEZ7"},{"id":"2Fi0lfLUzlGyHKvbraw5Z","type":"shape","kind":"rectangle","position":{"x":10720,"y":4770},"width":1720,"height":120,"fillColor":"#607d8b","text":"Facilitation guide","textFontFamily":"Inter","textAlignment":"left","attachedFrame":"tL4RwGWE8c7sGkjfrnwIA","textSize":56,"textColor":"#ffffff","textBold":true},{"id":"2Nd_DOWZgPEcmdJlHtf3W","type":"shape","kind":"rectangle","position":{"x":10740,"y":4940},"width":1680,"height":1060,"fillColor":"transparent","text":"🚀 Retrospective: How it works in 5 steps\n\n🎯 Purpose: Look back on a sprint, project or event and agree on improvements.\n\n1. Set the stage (5 min)\nAction: Name the period you are looking back on and agree to be open and respectful.\n\n2. Collect (10 min, silent)\nAction: Everyone writes cards for the quadrants:\nCONTINUE – what worked well and should stay?\nSTOP – what holds us back?\nINVENT – what new idea would we try with unlimited resources?\nRule: One point per card, use the matching colour stack.\n\n3. Present and cluster (15 min)\nAction: Each person briefly reads out their cards. Group similar cards.\n\n4. Prioritise (5 min)\nAction: Dot voting (e.g. 3 dots each) on the most important topics.\n\n5. Act (15 min)\nAction: For the top topics, define concrete steps in ACT: what, who, by when.\nGoal: 1–3 actions that are actually done before the next retro.\n\n🛠️ Your role as facilitator\nSafe space: Make sure nobody is blamed.\nTimekeeper: Protect enough time for the ACT quadrant.\nFollow-up: Start the next retro by checking last time's actions.","textFontFamily":"Inter","textAlignment":"left","attachedFrame":"tL4RwGWE8c7sGkjfrnwIA","textSize":24,"textColor":"#000000"}]}]}}